  "worked_solution": "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=-4(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x))^{5}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=-4{u}^{5},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=-20{u}^{4},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x).\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-20{u}^{4}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x)) \\\\  & =20{cos}^{4}\u2061(x)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
